--ROLES
-- Every spell gets exactly one bucket. Two consumers:
--   1. The panel's "by role" listing instead of "by class" (cosmetic).
--   2. The FOCUS TAX in Client.lua (balance). Each role has a healthy line count in
--      AP_HEALTHY; every line past it in the same role costs progressively more.
--
-- THIS FILE AFFECTS BALANCE. Retagging a spell moves it into a different role's
-- healthy-count budget and changes what builds are affordable. It is no longer the
-- browse-only file it started as -- check AP_HEALTHY in Client.lua before bulk edits.
--
-- Separate from categories.data, which taxes the ~84 known stacking exploits by a
-- different rule. The 8 exploit bucket names below (immunity, defensive_cd, raid_buff,
-- aoe_heal, mana_sustain, burst_cd, mobility, interrupt) are a superset of that file:
-- those lines are taxed on both axes, so their AP_HEALTHY allowances are set high
-- enough that the focus tax stays quiet until well past what categories.data prices.
--
-- Derived from Spell.dbc effect/aura data, so roughly 80% accurate: retag freely for
-- accuracy, but expect a balance effect when you do.

if CLDB==nil then CLDB={} end
if CLDB.roles==nil then CLDB.roles={} end

CLDB.roles={
